<title>JAPAN: Japan March nickel imports down 2.8 pct yr/yr--MOF.</title>
<headline>Japan March nickel imports down 2.8 pct yr/yr--MOF.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's refined nickel imports were down 2.8 percent to 4,604 tonnes in March from 4,735 tonnes in the same month a year earlier, Finance Ministry data released on Monday showed.</p>
<p>Details were as follows (on a customs-cleared basis, in</p>
<p>tonnes):</p>
<p>		   Mar 97    Feb 97     Mar 96</p>
<p> Total	   4,604     4,259	4,735</p>
<p>Major suppliers:</p>
<p> Russia	  1,301	 953	  817</p>
<p> S. Africa	 364	 340	  882</p>
<p> Zimbabwe	  240	 774	  383</p>
<p>Cumulative imports in the first three months of 1997 totalled 15,678 tonnes, up 3.7 percent from 15,121 tonnes in the same period a year earlier.</p>
<p>--Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3-3432-6179</p>
</text>
